<!-- =====================================================================
     PRJHW_fan - AyMON example: a fan that follows the temperature, on a
     Raspberry Pi's own pins, or on chips in memory when no parts are wired.

       FAN/S00   a thermistor and a knob through an ADC0834 (SPI), a fan
                 through an L293D (PWM), an LCD1602 (I2C), a push button
                 (an interrupt), and a page: http://127.0.0.1:8120/

     Runs as it is on any machine: every bus says con_host="sim:..".
     With the parts wired, three lines in db_FAN.xml change: see the README.

     Four connections, four devices, one document: inside the FREE edition.

     Run:  run.bat  or  ./run.sh,  then open  http://127.0.0.1:8120/
     ===================================================================== -->
